Playbook for Claude Code — Licence

Copyright (c) 2026 SparkYard.  All rights reserved.

DRAFT FOR REVIEW. This text is a plain-language starting point, not legal
advice. Have it reviewed before the first public release.

1. Use. You may download, install and use this software (the "Software"),
   free of charge, for personal or commercial work.

2. Restrictions. You may not, and may not let anyone else:
   a. copy the Software, except as needed to install and run it;
   b. modify, adapt, translate or create derivative works of it;
   c. reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble it, except to the extent
      the law where you live allows this despite this restriction;
   d. redistribute, publish, rent, lend, sublicense or sell it; or
   e. remove or change any notice of ownership in it.

3. Ownership. The Software is licensed, not sold. The copyright holder keeps
   all rights not expressly granted here.

4. Updates. The Software may check for and install new versions of itself.
   This licence covers those versions too, unless they come with a different
   licence.

5. No warranty. The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any
   kind, express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose.

6. Limitation of liability. To the extent the law allows, the copyright
   holder is not liable for any damages arising from the use of, or the
   inability to use, the Software.

7. Termination. This licence ends automatically if you break its terms.
   When it ends, you must stop using the Software and delete every copy.
